<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="ATasteOfHoney-Dm-Theme" spTempo="120">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1960
Composer:	Bobby Scott
Lyricist:	Ric Marlow
Form:	Irregular/through-composed instrumental
	theme; no universally standardized jazz
	form
Style:	Jazz-influenced pop ballad
Key:	D minor/Dorian
Arrangement:	Paul Desmond

“A Taste of Honey” was first written as an instrumental
theme for the 1960 Broadway production of the British
play of the same name. Ric Marlow later added lyrics,
making Bobby Scott and Marlow the official songwriting
team; the tune is often described as Dorian rather than
strictly major or minor. </spComments>
